// A2 course (A1 → A2 roadmap), module 13 „Töö ja amet” (a2-061…065), level A2, in the final shape
// (docs/COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_A2.md, row m13 = m5: AVAS LUGU PROB KUUL with the leads of modules 11–19; gates V1–V16 of
// docs/COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_B1.md §8). One storyline, one year before the B1 course (docs/COURSE_CAST.md): May. Sofia's money is running
// out and she looks for her first job in Estonia. Markus tells her that his firm Tuul Logistika (Peterburi tee 18) needs an office
// assistant. Saturday 8 May: the job fair at the culture house Sild, where she meets the head of the firm, Liis. Tuesday 11 May: the
// interview, the phone rings when Sofia is alone. Friday 14 May: two offers and a problem: Tuul Logistika (office, Mon–Fri 8.30–17, 1250 €,
// from 1 September) and Kaubahall through Anna (shifts, 950 €, from June); her Keelekool Sõna lessons are in the daytime. Ene has an evening
// course, Sofia chooses Tuul Logistika and helps at Kaubahall in the summer. Friday 28 May: the trial day with Liis's instructions. Liis is
// here what she is in the B1 course: Sofia's boss and nobody else. Pictures (art/visuals/a2-module-13.js): 062 Liis and Markus in
// the warehouse, 065 Anna and Markus compare their days.
//   061 AVAS R→S  try first → rule → try again: töötan müüjana, töötan poes, vastutan kaupade eest; corner R3 (signs at work, after 059's
//                 S2); main: the learner talks about a job at the fair stand (S01).
//   062 LUGU R→W  the interview, a story with a cliffhanger: pean + ma-vorm, ei pea, oskan / saan / tahan + da-vorm; corner W1 (a text
//                 from Liis's business card); main: the end of the story, 60–80 words (W05); home recording: the picture (S06).
//   063 PROB L→S  two offers: kella kaheksast viieni, E–R, vahetus, palk, kogemus, vajalik, kandideerima; first try, language, second try;
//                 corner L4 (a talk, matching); main: the pair agrees which job fits (S03); then the call to Ene (S04).
//   064 KUUL L→W  the trial day: alusta, too, vii, helista, kontrolli, ära unusta; alustage, tooge; corner L3 (Liis's instructions, short
//                 answers); main: a 50–70-word letter to Kati (W04), planned first.
//   065 EKS       the module exam, every part timed (B.examPart): R1–R5, L1–L4, W1, W2a, S0, S1, S2.
// Every teaching lesson: „Mäletad?” naming the previous lesson and one of modules 10–11, an in-lesson pair task, a home
// recording in Kasuta, two fluency tasks, one exam corner. No tingiv kõneviis (A2).
